               <h3>Childrens Pastor</h3>
               <div id="bio"> 
               	 <img src="images/cp.jpg" alt="Childrens Pastor Lisa Whitmire" width=260 height=260 />
                    <p><strong>Childrens Pastor Lisa Whitmire</strong> <i>(...or better known as "Mrs. Lisa")</i> is the Children&lsquo;s Pastor at New Life Worship Center.  She has been in children&lsquo;s ministry for more than 28 years.  As a young teenager, she helped her mom teach children. By the age of 16 she was helping full-time and by age 18 she was running the entire children&lsquo;s ministry.  "I was young", she says, "but God is so amazing.  It is just proof that He only needs a willing vessel and He will fill it and equip it."  She has been a part of New Life Worship Center for 17 years.  Mrs. Lisa and her husband Scott have been married for 25 years.  They have 3 children, Chris, Alyssa, and Phillip.  They reside in Union Grove, Texas.  Scott works as a printer and Mrs. Lisa works part-time for Mayhan Fabricators as a receptionist.</p>
                    <p>"I collect teddy bears and love old Elvis movies and songs!  Scott even sang one to me on our wedding day!  I love being a wife, mom, friend, sister, aunt, daughter, and Children&lsquo;s Pastor!!!  And I love the idea of kids getting to know Jesus.  I mean KNOW Jesus, not just know OF Him... Kids are amazing little people.  Full of innocence, wonder, amazement, life, and laughter.  Their eyes light up when you tell them something amazing about God.  They believe it.  They can live it!  I thank God for the calling He has placed on my life to be a part of their amazing adventure to find Him for themselves."</p>
                    <h4><i>~Mission Statement~</i></h4>
                    <p>"The mission of the children&lsquo;s ministry of New Life Worship Center is to bring Jesus to life in the lives of every child that we come in contact with.. In a world full of stress, hurt, situations out of their control, and superheroes who are only alive in their imagination, we want to give them something and someone that they can believe in and put their trust in that truly lives.  To help them build a deep and strong relationship with Jesus Christ now so that they can stand as strong boys and girls in every circumstance that comes their way. To love every child that comes through our doors, even if it&lsquo;s only once, so they can encounter Jesus through our words, and our touch, leaving them longing for something more of Him.  They will be a diverse group of children made up of all cultures and backgrounds.  They will fill the children&lsquo;s sanctuary with life and laughter, and most importantly they will move in the presence of God as He falls on us every week.  When these kids leave our ministry and move into the youth group, they will already be mighty warriors for God, rooted and grounded deeply in the words of truth, never to be swayed by sin!"</p>
                    <h4>- Children&lsquo;s Pastor Lisa Whitmire</h4>
